.TH SPACESCAN 1 "2026-10-17" "SpaceScan 1.1.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
spacescan \- see what takes the space on your disks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spacescan
.RI [ "APP OPTIONS" ]
.RI [ PATH ]
.br
.B spacescan
.I COMMAND PATH
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B SpaceScan
scans a drive, mount point or folder and shows where the space went, as an
interactive sunburst chart or as a table driven from the keyboard. Files
are grouped by category (video, audio, images, code and others), with
filters by name, size and date. Files can be moved to the trash, deleted,
copied and moved; anything that is or contains a mounted filesystem is
never deleted.
.PP
Without a
.IR COMMAND ,
.B spacescan
opens its window, and scans
.I PATH
right away when one is given. With a
.IR COMMAND ,
it writes a report of
.I PATH
to standard output and opens no window.
.SH APP OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-category " NAME,NAME"
Show only these categories' files. Names are as the app shows them in its
language, in any case.
.TP
.BI \-\-filter " TEXT"
Start with this name filter, as typed in the app's Filters window, for
example
.BR "*.log,*.tmp" .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
The folders and files directly in
.IR PATH ,
with their totals.
.TP
.B flat
Every file under
.IR PATH ,
in all its subfolders.
.TP
.B exts
File extensions under
.IR PATH ,
with their sizes and file counts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-format " txt|csv|json"
Output format (default: txt).
.TP
.BR \-\-sort " size|files|name|modified|changed"
Order of
.B list
and
.B flat
(default: size;
.B files
applies to
.B list
only).
.TP
.BR \-\-by " bytes|files"
Order of
.B exts
(default: bytes).
.TP
.B \-\-reverse
Reverse the order.
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " N"
.BR flat :
only the first
.I N
files.
.TP
.B \-\-apparent\-size
Count file lengths instead of disk space used.
.TP
.BI \-\-filter " TEXT"
Only files whose names match, as in the app's Filters window; folders count
only those files.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.PP
Sizes in CSV and JSON are in bytes; times are local, as
YYYY\-MM\-DDTHH:MM:SS\(+-HH:MM. Names that aren't valid UTF\-8 are shown
escaped, as in the app (\exFF).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. Unreadable subfolders are reported on standard error but don't
fail the run.
.TP
.B 1
The folder can't be read, or standard output is closed.
.TP
.B 2
A mistake on the command line.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/spacescan/settings.json
Settings, saved from the app's Settings window.
.TP
.I ~/.config/spacescan/categories.json
File categories and their extensions, written with the defaults on first
start and read again at every scan.
.TP
.I ~/.config/spacescan/lang/
Language files that add a language or change lines of a built-in one.
.SH EXAMPLES
The 20 biggest files in the Downloads folder:
.PP
.RS
.B spacescan flat ~/Downloads \-\-limit 20
.RE
.PP
A spreadsheet of what's in the home folder:
.PP
.RS
.B spacescan list ~ \-\-format csv > home.csv
.RE
.PP
The app, showing only the videos in the home folder:
.PP
.RS
.B spacescan \-\-category video ~
.RE
